 ## [Unreleased]
 
+- **Keep built-in navigation consistent.** Call hierarchy and declaration tabs retain the selected PHP version’s signatures and source locations after other files are opened. Embedded declarations remain read-only. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
 - **Follow literal callable strings in call hierarchy.** Direct function and static-method strings retain their runtime target and exact invocation site, including deprecated public trait calls. Ordinary class calls outside a class now preserve the enclosing namespace when a global class has the same short name. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
 
 - **Follow quoted method selectors.** Navigation, references and call hierarchy recognize fixed string method names. Rename includes escaped names while preserving quotes and refuses references whose source changed. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
